{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/legal/terms.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:05:22.991563Z","id":"08f08d856553785c57df55b4c735be8b43b36fe61ac8a73b292523183bd88c03","body":{"detail":"docs/legal/terms.md and docs/legal/privacy.md adapt Pathbase's (../pathbase/web/content/legal/, last updated May 2026) to Clax, without legal review. Open: (1) counsel review of both. (2) They name the hosted service at https://clax.dev, operated by Empathic Inc.; confirm that is the service and its operator. (3) Pathbase's tos@pathbase.dev and dmca@pathbase.dev became contact@empathic.dev (DMCA with 'DMCA' in the subject); create clax-specific mailboxes if wanted. (4) Pathbase's terms 7.1(b) let Empathic use de-identified User Content to improve AI models; the Clax terms drop it and the privacy policy says User Content is not used to train AI models. Keep or reverse. (5) The terms point at https://clax.dev/privacy, which the hosted shell does not serve: the hosted UI needs /terms and /privacy pages, links from sign-in and setup, and possibly acceptance at sign-up or setup (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs, web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte); a UI change whose design questions are the owner's. (6) Pathbase's rules against copying, reverse engineering and mirroring were dropped or narrowed, since the Clax software is GPL-2.0/AGPL-3.0; the terms cover only the hosted service.","kind":"concern","summary":"Before publishing the hosted terms and privacy policy: counsel review, the clax.dev operator, mailboxes, AI training, and serving them in the hosted UI","tags":["status:needs-decision","legal","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/legal/terms.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:43:35.961749Z","id":"c833a0cd9493aa00b580b24bf16175ebaeade1bc7f68a980b17d30746cc7dcc9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"08f08d856553785c57df55b4c735be8b43b36fe61ac8a73b292523183bd88c03","summary":"Serving them in the hosted UI landed in 278232cc0: legal = \"bundled\" ([hosted], or LEGAL / deploy.mjs --legal bundled on the Worker) serves /terms and /privacy from these files, the sign-in pages say signing in agrees to them, legal_agreements (migration 39) records each agreement, and a person who has not agreed to BUNDLED_LEGAL_VERSION (crates/clax-core/src/config.rs) is asked once. clax.dev shows them only once deployed with --legal bundled. Counsel review, the operator, the mailboxes and the AI-training clause remain open here.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/legal/terms.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:48:32.403553Z","id":"4750feda196ba7e525f14a9a44816c3ca4c928e95d1e32a5cf6f30c22be836c6","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:7ce09bede","references":"08f08d856553785c57df55b4c735be8b43b36fe61ac8a73b292523183bd88c03","summary":"Decided by the owner: (2) Empathic Inc. operates the hosted service at clax.dev, as the documents say. (4) Keep Pathbase's permission: the terms grant Empathic use of aggregated or de-identified User Content to improve its services and AI models (terms 7.1(b), 9), and the privacy policy lists that use (7ce09bede). Open: (1) counsel review, (3) mailboxes, (6) the narrowed copying and reverse-engineering rules.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/legal/terms.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:48.747136Z","id":"e0d62e5eb08659152221d36f32686e7f6573309c8b8d581bf258f882e3613cc1","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:24e68a914","references":"08f08d856553785c57df55b4c735be8b43b36fe61ac8a73b292523183bd88c03","summary":"Decided by the owner: the documents follow Pathbase's as closely as they can, with no mention of the Clax software's licenses. The Privacy Policy is Pathbase's word for word; the Terms are Pathbase's with Clax, clax.dev, the date and contact@empathic.dev for tos@ and dmca@pathbase.dev (952c5b943, 24e68a914). (6) is settled: Pathbase's rules against reproducing, reverse engineering, mirroring, downloading and scraping apply to Clax, defined as the platform at clax.dev. Open: (1) counsel review, (3) whether to have Clax mailboxes.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
